# Backend Development Rules

## Code Style
- TypeScript strict mode — no `any` types unless absolutely unavoidable
- Async/await over callbacks or raw promises
- Zod schemas for all data structures that cross boundaries
- Fastify patterns (register, decorators, schemas) — NOT Express

## Service Pattern (MANDATORY)
Every backend module MUST extend `BaseService` and register in `ServiceContainer`:

```typescript
import { BaseService } from '../services/base-service';

export class MyService extends BaseService {
  protected async _construct(): Promise<void> {
    // Set up data structures. No cross-service deps here.
  }

  protected async _init(): Promise<void> {
    // Wire to other services. this.services.get('name') works here.
  }

  protected async _destroy(): Promise<void> {
    // Cleanup: close connections, clear intervals.
  }
}
```

Register in boot sequence: `container.register('my-service', new MyService('my-service'))`

## SSH Rules
- Use `ssh2` directly — NOT node-ssh or wrappers
- `exec()` for one-shot data collection (parallel, ephemeral channels)
- `shell()` for interactive terminal (persistent, one per connection)
- `sftp()` for file operations (lazy-initialized, reused)
- NEVER run `exec('cat ...',)` for file reads — use SFTP

## Parsing Pipeline
All command output goes through `ParsingPipeline.parse()`:
1. Strip ANSI via `strip-ansi`
2. Try deterministic parser (regex, <1ms, free)
3. Fall back to LLM (1-3s, costs money)
4. Validate with Zod schema

## Command Orchestrator
Multi-command views use `CommandOrchestrator.execute()`:
- Define an `ExecutionPlan` with steps
- Steps run in parallel unless `dependsOn` is specified
- On parse failure → retry with Zod error context
- On command failure → try `fallbackCommands`

## Security
- NEVER interpolate user input into shell commands: `exec(\`rm ${userPath}\`)` ← BANNED
- Validate: paths (no `../`), container IDs (hex only), PIDs (integer only)
- Command allowlists for any dynamic command execution
- See `docs/SECURITY.md` for full rules

## File Locations
| Purpose | Path |
|---------|------|
| Entry point | `server/src/index.ts` |
| Services | `server/src/services/` |
| SSH | `server/src/ssh/connection-manager.ts` |
| Orchestrator | `server/src/orchestrator/orchestrator.ts` |
| LLM interface | `server/src/llm/provider.ts` |
| LLM providers | `server/src/llm/providers/` |
| Parsing pipeline | `server/src/parsers/pipeline.ts` |
| Deterministic parsers | `server/src/parsers/deterministic/` |
| Zod schemas | `server/src/parsers/schemas/` |
| API routes | `server/src/routes/` |
| Config store | `server/src/config/store.ts` |
